@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Data Policy";
}

<div class="dash-header" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div>
        <h1 class="dash-title">Data Policy</h1>
        <p class="dash-subtitle">How FashionBI collects, processes, and protects retail analytics data</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="max-width:860px;padding:32px 36px;line-height:1.75;">

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">1. Scope</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        FashionBI is a retail business intelligence platform designed for internal use by authorised
        retail analysts. It aggregates product, sales, and inventory data from connected store
        systems for the purpose of performance monitoring, demand forecasting, and sustainability
        reporting.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">2. Data Collected</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        The platform synchronises the following categories of operational data from connected
        store APIs: product catalogue (codes, categories, pricing), sales transactions (order
        identifiers, quantities, revenue, channel), inventory levels (stock counts, reorder
        thresholds), and store metadata (name, location, type). No personal customer data
        is collected or stored.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">3. Data Storage</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        All data is stored in a SQL Server database hosted within the organisation's own
        infrastructure. The platform does not transmit operational data to third-party services.
        Forecast model outputs are persisted locally and are not shared externally.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">4. Access Control</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        Access to the platform is restricted to authenticated users. Sessions are secured with
        HTTP-only cookies and expire after 8 hours of inactivity. All analytics endpoints
        require authentication; unauthenticated requests are redirected to the sign-in page.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">5. Data Retention</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        Operational data is retained for the duration required to support the configured
        analytics windows (up to 24 months of historical sales for ABC/XYZ analysis and
        forecasting). Data may be removed by an administrator at any time through the
        database management interface.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">6. Machine Learning</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:20px;">
        The Forecasting module runs a Random Forest regression model locally using historical
        sales data. Training and inference occur entirely on-premises. No data is sent to
        external model APIs or cloud inference services.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;">7. Contact</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);">
        Questions regarding data handling should be directed to the platform administrator
        responsible for this deployment.
    </p>

</div>
